## Context
padme PR #133 (2026-10-28, one line in `intervention-log.txt`) could not pass verify-gate. Gaze ran twice, both
REVIEWED, and verify-gate refused admission both times: `review_notes.py gate rv-20261028-pr-133-9b75 <head>` exited 1
with "no full review: the delta answer covering the head does not carry an earlier full answer (coverage.carried)".
The author merged without the gate on an explicit decision (comment on the PR).

Notes on padme `refs/notes/review`:
- answer `20261028T111032959Z-padme-7df2567a` at 171a0eb, the first review of the PR: `coverage: {scope: delta,
  carried: null}`;
- answer `20261028T111308087Z-padme-4af4bb66` at e1b6fd4, asked in the brief as "FULL review (not delta) of the whole
  PR diff": `coverage: {scope: delta, carried: <the first>}`.

Cause (read, not yet reproduced in a test): `scripts/gaze_close.py` `answer_scope()` returns `full` only when the result
carries `scope: full` or `intent: default`; any other intent records `delta` (spec §4, "a narrow intent is never
widened"). A caller that passes a descriptive intent (every gaze call in that session did: "measurement-only PR…",
"FULL review of the whole PR diff…") therefore gets a delta on a first review, `carry_target` finds nothing to carry,
and `_full_or_chained` can never be satisfied: the PR is unadmittable however many times gaze reruns. PRs #128–#131 in
the same session passed only because their gate runs went through other admission paths; not yet checked which.

The attribution failures seen in the same runs (bare `gpt-6-luna`, `model=script`) are ticket 1303, not this one.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A test replays the #133 shape: no prior answer, a caller intent that is not `default`, result REVIEWED;
      verify-gate admission then succeeds (or gaze refuses up front and says how to ask for a full review).
- [ ] The rule for when an intent is narrow (delta) versus whole-diff (full) is written in gaze `SKILL.md`, and a
      caller can state it without knowing the `intent: default` keyword.
- [ ] A delta answer with `carried: null` is never written silently: gaze either records it as full (nothing earlier
      to be a delta of) or reports it as unadmittable in its result.

